    "terrainName": "berlin",
    "description": "What: Simulated devices SD-S5b (§5a, D-119). The Observer carries a laser rangefinder (kit 1) LINKED to the binoculars A (kit 2 - paired back to it), and binoculars B (kit 3) that no link names. A scripted trainee possesses him, ranges a marker 450 m away through the rangefinder, presses its SEND chip, then binds his view to the binoculars A. Judge: (1) before SEND the binoculars A hold no target; (2) one tick after SEND they hold the marker's point (within 2 m), its range (~450 m), the sender's TKB type and the sender's name, as the rangefinder measured it; (3) their HUD shows the received-target cue - TARGET, and the sender line 'from LASER RANGEFINDER (linked)'; (4) the binoculars B - not addressed - never receive anything. Fail: the point lost or wrong, a cue that is not drawn, or a message that reaches a device nobody addressed. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh dv-linked-target"
  },
